---
// An illustration of what the free video audit looks like: a recorded walkthrough of the
// practitioner's site with Matt narrating and notes on what to fix. Drawn in HTML/CSS.
import { asset } from "../lib";
---
<figure class="audit-mock">
  <div class="am-window" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="am-bar">
      <span class="am-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
      <span class="am-url">yourpractice.com</span>
    </div>
    <div class="am-page">
      <div class="am-nav"><span class="am-logo"></span><span class="am-links"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span></div>
      <div class="am-hero">
        <p class="am-h">Welcome to my practice</p>
        <span class="am-line w80"></span><span class="am-line w60"></span>
        <span class="am-btn">Contact</span>
      </div>
      <div class="am-cols"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>

      <span class="am-note n1"><b>1</b>Say what you do and where. Add your city to this heading.</span>
      <span class="am-note n2"><b>2</b>Your booking button is easy to miss.</span>
      <span class="am-note n3"><b>3</b>This page could rank for “eating disorder therapist near me.”</span>

      <img class="am-face" src={asset("matt.jpg")} alt="" width="96" height="96" loading="lazy" />
    </div>
    <div class="am-player">
      <span class="am-play"></span>
      <span class="am-track"><span></span></span>
      <span class="am-time">1:42 / 4:32</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figcaption>An example of what you’ll receive: a short, personal video walking through your site, with the top things we’d fix first.</figcaption>
</figure>
